#edb/ref 17592186351841} {:answer/id #uuid "8ccb0ed8-c244-526d-bd95-0afe4b9f1d20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352793} {:answer/id #uuid "94fa75b7-cafb-5ad1-9ce5-95bfd9f279aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352860} {:answer/id #uuid "c5c6c424-44a6-5b78-8fe2-df9d8d43c572" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353281} {:answer/id #uuid "d42fdac2-d497-5c59-9f09-cf3689d2916a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{7}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351841} :answer-field/id #uuid "2eddccc9-cdd9-5789-8c66-c51a64ee156f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353895}] :question/id #uuid "95714e1c-2016-579b-bc67-9386a69d2d7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-86848" :question/problem "$$\nV=\\text{Span}{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ \\sqrt{7}\\end{bmatrix}},\\,B={\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $V$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $V,$ given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{b}{a}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's denote \n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ \\sqrt{7}\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{3\\cdot (-1)+(-2)\\cdot 5+\\sqrt{7}\\cdot 0}{(-1)^{2}+{5}^{2}+{0}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ \\sqrt{7}\\end{bmatrix}+\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{7}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B={{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}={\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{7}\\end{bmatrix}}$ is an orthogonal basis for $V.$\n\nFinally, we have $a=\\frac{5}{2},$ $b=\\frac{1}{2},$ and \n\n$$\n\\frac{b}{a}=\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{(\\frac{5}{2})}=\\frac{1}{5}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414751 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18fa685c-26d9-50c3-9545-5630e0f95fcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414724} {:answer/id #uuid "194427ad-263d-5d8c-83c2-9e6a530a1d0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414725} {:answer/id #uuid "5c1253b4-be89-5b75-90d7-9bf16f52d17f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414729} {:answer/id #uuid "a926e36b-6239-5512-942a-761db7b00ee5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414740} {:answer/id #uuid "f308a53e-6685-5d66-b2f6-d1b95a0af889" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414744}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414729} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ce877fc-f404-5538-a461-7601462b178c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414748}] :question/id #uuid "44c51145-6075-534b-b54c-46371542f3eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-40737" :question/problem "$$\nV=\\text{Span}\\{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\},\\,B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $V$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $V,$ given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{b}{a}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's denote \n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{4\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot (-1)}{{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\}$ is an orthogonal basis for $V.$\n\nFinally, we have $a=-\\frac{1}{2},$ $b=2,$ and \n\n$$\n\\frac{b}{a}=\\frac{2}{(-\\frac{1}{2})}=-4.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414753 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "048ef5c8-0a10-53a5-bbcf-1d721a524144" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414721} {:answer/id #uuid "05da9795-05f5-5040-9da5-00cee056fe08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414722} {:answer/id #uuid "1326ecd9-681d-55f9-841c-c7013851f621" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414723} {:answer/id #uuid "292aa1fd-4f1b-5b3f-b502-e340aa086aa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414726} {:answer/id #uuid "502fbad5-6108-585e-9a6e-c3c7e917352d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414723} :answer-field/id #uuid "219cb7dd-0360-5f51-af53-0c31b7c77c47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414745}] :question/id #uuid "c7bb7823-c38b-5250-a2f7-3b306162dae1" :question/math-academy-id "q-40736" :question/problem "$$\nV=\\text{Span}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}},\\,B={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $V$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $V,$ given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's denote \n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{3\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 1+2\\cdot (-2)}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{17}{6} \\\\ \\frac{11}{6} \\\\ \\frac{7}{3}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B={{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{17}{6} \\\\ \\frac{11}{6} \\\\ \\frac{7}{3}\\end{bmatrix}}$ is an orthogonal basis for $V.$\n\nFinally, we have $a=\\frac{17}{6},$ $b=\\frac{11}{6},$ and \n\n$$\n\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{(\\frac{17}{6})}{(\\frac{11}{6})}=\\frac{17}{11}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481350 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35fb792f-f499-55f0-beb5-0a36ea500f74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480845} {:answer/id #uuid "391ed7ae-6243-537b-a07f-f3dade005876" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480852} {:answer/id #uuid "8fdbf6e7-3003-543d-b80a-6884375af46b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481009} {:answer/id #uuid "91a07927-047f-58d6-9e1b-00da5c4d3b96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481011} {:answer/id #uuid "b06c78e9-7124-5c1a-ba75-ab5286b77cd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481072} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5e8feed-0144-5565-9376-5bcd8f09bbb0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481303}] :question/id #uuid "17e0153f-17ba-57ee-a920-3117ebdc5b12" :question/math-academy-id "q-140524" :question/problem "$$\nV=\\text{Span}\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\},\\,B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $V$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $V,$ given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{b}{a}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-1)}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}$ is an orthogonal basis for $V.$\n\nFinally, $a=1,$ $b=-2,$ and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{b}{a}=\\frac{-2}{1}=-2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481360 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d9e8e1d-513e-59b9-9746-2585e1481503" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480764} {:answer/id #uuid "2466579e-51e6-5724-b11f-494b5cbd91ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480807} {:answer/id #uuid "5e2dc305-ac17-582b-9568-ed63665348b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480914} {:answer/id #uuid "67ccaa28-3669-5421-86da-e8251e588b2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480931} {:answer/id #uuid "d058a80e-4564-5675-b58b-217af9b2adce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480914} :answer-field/id #uuid "363499bf-09e7-5ef8-9f85-08b9df560e62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481258}] :question/id #uuid "41cad912-e122-5581-bcb3-a15aeb801b3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-41031" :question/problem "$$\nV=\\text{Span}\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\},\\,B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $V$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $V,$ given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{c}{a}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{4\\cdot 1+0\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 1}{{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}$ is an orthogonal basis for $V.$\n\nFinally, $a=3,$ $c=1,$ and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{c}{a}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481363 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16f8819e-1e45-5b70-843f-9474e62016e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480782} {:answer/id #uuid "2dcb854a-8359-5e93-87cf-89bffc23af38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480823} {:answer/id #uuid "30e0bd06-5ba4-5322-8aaa-c8efbd6bb22c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480832} {:answer/id #uuid "54604561-d490-5cf0-8396-166d4506693f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480890} {:answer/id #uuid "8567ab33-79b0-5c93-ab46-2e6895393cb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186480782} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1c3af90-4b4e-5817-986c-ad8b162022f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481335}] :question/id #uuid "4b9728bb-13e5-5813-917f-2ed0c37ac7bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-86847" :question/problem "$$\nV=\\text{Span}\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\},\\,B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $V$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $V,$ given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{c}{a}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's denote \n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{(-1)\\cdot (-3)+0\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2}{(-3)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}$ is an orthogonal basis for $V.$\n\nFinally, we have $a=\\frac{1}{2},$ $c=1,$ and \n\n$$\n\\frac{c}{a}=\\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{2})}=2.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Orthogonal Basis For the Span of Two Vectors"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133794 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133603 :question/id #uuid "47fadc87-f265-5f1c-827a-28e5be9e8121" :question/math-academy-id "e-5582" :question/problem "Consider the subspace $\\textrm{Col}(A)$ and an orthogonal basis $\\mathcal B$ of $\\textrm{Col}(A),$ where $A$ and $\\mathcal B$ are given below. Given that $\\mathcal B$ is derived from $\\textrm{Col}(A)$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\dfrac{c}{a}?$\n\n![](images/b2/b20aeaf492050b26176c993d64442f214c39d24092989ec1c75b5e2ca9673947.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\textrm{Col}(A)$ is the span of the columns of $A.$  \n\nFirst, let's denote\n\n![](images/fa/fa7bd1a6125c6796bd5689409a22c34081e78027dbaff1356efecddfe755b323.svg)\n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n- **Step 1**: We set ![](images/0f/0f65ef9e505d3e961d0330c1ff6d52d5239eff91811a61b4878d6a2f13923bff.svg)\n\n- **Step 2**: Next, we find $\\mathbf{v}_2$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for $\\mathbf v_2$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{(-5)\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot 2}{{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](images/be/be2842c481ecd55360f9bc3054e2535d4a92bbb8ebd77f169522c329ff2d715d.svg) is an orthogonal basis for $\\textrm{Col}(A).$\n\nFinally, $a=-4,$ $c=-1,$ and  \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{c}{a} = \\dfrac{-1}{-4} = \\dfrac{1}{4}.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b15719b6-0ce4-5fb8-80be-abcaf9344a10" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134312 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02a9e964-e971-5a63-8ddf-d35611c16d45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323997} {:answer/id #uuid "3b6569f2-157f-59bd-b487-d77abba9f8d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324450} {:answer/id #uuid "4ee6004c-940f-594a-9082-a66d246e0808" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324618} {:answer/id #uuid "7e307e2d-eb04-5931-a49e-da669978c621" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325033} {:answer/id #uuid "c2a72c2b-2e25-5ac5-9983-7b64eb42b19a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324618} :answer-field/id #uuid "67bfe10d-3e1e-5ac4-80e9-14d87bdcdeaa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326398}] :question/id #uuid "5fc90254-ed2d-508a-b704-d310ff8d6596" :question/math-academy-id "q-40741" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $\\text{Col}(A)$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ where $A$ and $B$ are given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $\\text{Col}(A)$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{b}{a}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{Col}(A)$ is the span of the columns of $A.$ \n\nFirst, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{2\\cdot 3+1\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot 0}{{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\}$ is an orthogonal basis for $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\nFinally, $a=\\frac{1}{2},$ $b=\\frac{3}{2},$ and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{b}{a}=\\frac{(\\frac{3}{2})}{(\\frac{1}{2})}=3.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134337 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a4ef1ec-81c9-56a1-ae34-cb378d16c96d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324192} {:answer/id #uuid "430eea34-b9a8-5fef-bc38-a0f1f469732d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324511} {:answer/id #uuid "9a68d292-ed71-5037-9830-282f02bf1b9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325285} {:answer/id #uuid "e0be4312-70a5-5ab1-8300-0bd829a9efc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325935} {:answer/id #uuid "e56aef94-f137-55ff-ac81-7fd165ea233c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325992} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccec1e07-b398-56bb-a890-6a479af9136d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326590}] :question/id #uuid "4388fdfa-5eb8-5165-a253-2f6080a33d4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-41035" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $\\text{Col}(A)$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ where $A$ and $B$ are given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $\\text{Col}(A)$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{c}{a}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{Col}(A)$ is the span of the columns of $A.$  \n\nFirst, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{5\\cdot 4+5\\cdot 4+(-2)\\cdot 2}{{4}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\\}$ is an orthogonal basis for $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\nFinally, $a=1,$ $c=-4,$ and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{c}{a}=\\frac{-4}{1}=-4.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272123 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c5324c4-d372-51db-b80e-57310ecef452" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269376} {:answer/id #uuid "2b563aea-36bf-58e1-85e1-370632786989" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269659} {:answer/id #uuid "339f0949-f255-5abb-92bb-95bd0cafba47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269740} {:answer/id #uuid "4e62fc44-ef13-513b-9718-e526f4879824" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269977} {:answer/id #uuid "b9c5a456-558c-5e5d-b7c5-b3d293046719" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269977} :answer-field/id #uuid "8085e6de-aa0c-5e0f-84f3-9fd3a3ba5f78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271735}] :question/id #uuid "395132aa-e570-57bb-9869-07e6441f4e7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-140526" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $\\text{Col}(A)$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ where $A$ and $B$ are given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $\\text{Col}(A)$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{a}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{Col}(A)$ is the span of the columns of $A.$  \n\nFirst, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{4\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 2}{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\}$ is an orthogonal basis for $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\nFinally, $a=2,$ $c=-1,$ and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{a}{c}=\\frac{2}{-1}=-2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272125 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02cd50ee-7dfb-5329-b414-a7e29e6d91af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269294} {:answer/id #uuid "0e3ed43b-9eec-5604-965c-4bda6251204f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269393} {:answer/id #uuid "71430654-a5e1-51d5-b25d-4d132a09c4f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270275} {:answer/id #uuid "8b96600f-4cfc-560d-a286-0ee5f9d41773" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270478} {:answer/id #uuid "d5cb0b79-a29d-51af-b029-65c79862a96d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271144} :answer-field/id #uuid "61209408-2d37-576f-b6f0-97778128a9a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271683}] :question/id #uuid "915cd440-9e70-527f-ae9d-6fd020966a43" :question/math-academy-id "q-140529" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $\\text{Col}(A)$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ where $A$ and $B$ are given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $\\text{Col}(A)$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{Col}(A)$ is the span of the columns of $A.$ \n\nFirst, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{2\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 3}{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B={{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}}$ is an orthogonal basis for $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\nFinally, $b=2,$ $c=-\\frac{1}{2},$ and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{b}{c}=\\frac{2}{(-\\frac{1}{2})}=-4.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326873 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10cc83e4-4a68-52d4-b338-032fbdc0c4f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324125} {:answer/id #uuid "3f470bd7-a807-5528-acc5-2a476fd2064d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324480} {:answer/id #uuid "712b96f9-5e05-5d1a-bb65-c463f83dfa57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324904} {:answer/id #uuid "af04c33b-d58b-555f-af8d-a4f9508a0b5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325459} {:answer/id #uuid "bf00d910-6f67-537f-8bac-b8822a589211" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325614} :answer-field/id #uuid "180276bb-da02-5515-9e1f-76b1748b74f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326266}] :question/id #uuid "d8c7811a-eb0e-522e-b483-fedac22b4a18" :question/math-academy-id "q-40742" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $\\text{Col}(A)$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ where $A$ and $B$ are given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $\\text{Col}(A)$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{Col}(A)$ is the span of the columns of $A.$ \n\nFirst, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{(-3)\\cdot 2+4\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 4}{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{4}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+\\frac{2}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ \\frac{10}{3} \\\\ \\frac{5}{3}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ \\frac{10}{3} \\\\ \\frac{5}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\}$ is an orthogonal basis for $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\nFinally, $b=\\frac{10}{3},$ $c=\\frac{5}{3},$ and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{b}{c}=\\frac{(\\frac{10}{3})}{(\\frac{5}{3})}=2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326899 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47d1854d-6fd6-526c-b759-d1209df8a9d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324552} {:answer/id #uuid "5eb14860-141a-5eac-b5fb-ef7a435dbf1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324759} {:answer/id #uuid "73d43e73-deae-5a38-b655-86047022d339" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324933} {:answer/id #uuid "aea345a6-603e-546e-ada6-149d72b91b04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325455} {:answer/id #uuid "c3c622cf-8e52-56ac-bc00-2f9457c767f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324933} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9ffb187-0527-51f3-b27a-ee8fed1376f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326526}] :question/id #uuid "4c9da90f-19cf-5646-82a3-18682358ed1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-41034" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $\\text{Col}(A)$ and an orthogonal basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ where $A$ and $B$ are given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $\\text{Col}(A)$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{b}{a}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{Col}(A)$ is the span of the columns of $A.$  \n\nFirst, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{4\\cdot 3+0\\cdot \\sqrt{3}+7\\cdot 0}{{3}^{2}+(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{0}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\\}$ is an orthogonal basis for $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\nFinally, $a=1,$ $b=-\\sqrt{3},$ and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{b}{a}=\\frac{-\\sqrt{3}}{1}=-\\sqrt{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351263 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05279c88-25ab-5a54-aa56-e1c60f9aa5fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348493} {:answer/id #uuid "1fd86a7e-ebb1-5da0-bac2-0d8d9bae3547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348722} {:answer/id #uuid "751c6092-53d7-5c48-bc24-abed2d5cb212" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349522} {:answer/id #uuid "90b55236-9748-5bf7-bc28-e5120721cb76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349747} {:answer/id #uuid "b7f2495a-31fd-513b-b278-24a29310f2a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350075} :answer-field/id #uuid "56b31e20-02a7-56ce-9f42-143b07559366" :answer-fi