from left to right, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ $2\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357672 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01cb3824-5a7b-5084-94cf-05aea0106386" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354669} {:answer/id #uuid "0f5269d3-bf8b-529c-b45d-9164b92e7a7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ and ${x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354806} {:answer/id #uuid "9738fdb2-48da-5c41-8ac0-fd42e5c81110" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and ${x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355992} {:answer/id #uuid "98a0ba9b-ca40-5b64-978c-9d5cf0f9e006" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ and ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356015} {:answer/id #uuid "dcd72186-76bc-5c2b-b651-28994adf6068" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ and ${x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ and ${x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354806} :answer-field/id #uuid "375043e1-8292-5bf0-abcd-e03b8b54889c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357008}] :question/id #uuid "cbcd8ba7-4396-5373-bfbd-def95f4d316f" :question/math-academy-id "q-94149" :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}+38{x}_{2}^{2}+16{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,{y}_{1}^{2}+6{y}_{2}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2} &={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what is missing from the blank spaces?" :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{1}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+38{x}_{2}^{2}+16{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\  & =(2{x}_{1}^{2}+16{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+38{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2({x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+38{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+38{x}_{2}^{2} & =2([{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+16{x}_{2}^{2}]-16{x}_{2}^{2})+38{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2(({x}_{1}+4{x}_{2})^{2}-16{x}_{2}^{2})+38{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(({x}_{1}+4{x}_{2})^{2}-16{x}_{2}^{2})+38{x}_{2}^{2} & =2({x}_{1}+4{x}_{2})^{2}-32{x}_{2}^{2}+38{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2({x}_{1}+4{x}_{2})^{2}+6{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n2{y}_{1}^{2}+6{y}_{2}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &={x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2} &={x}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ $2\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371838 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e26ecbc9-5f55-5fc2-b913-e0387bae1a00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2$ and $2{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371840} {:answer/id #uuid "664a31f2-dfe8-55b1-9927-ffb98e96624f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ and ${x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371841} {:answer/id #uuid "5a1495ac-6d98-5a1e-9189-9359f9d03e56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ and ${x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371842} {:answer/id #uuid "5836c75e-feb6-51de-b630-ec3c2f5879f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ and ${x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371843} {:answer/id #uuid "6bce7b9a-ebd9-5c44-88e3-05dcbe850100" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ and ${x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371841} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd266aaa-1caa-513d-bc03-2d70675b060c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371839}] :question/id #uuid "84c351a9-3188-5518-acd0-538fa9cf47e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-140983" :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}+9{x}_{2}^{2}-8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n2{y}_{1}^{2}+\\boxed{}\\,{y}_{2}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2} &={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what is missing from the blank spaces?" :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{1}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+9{x}_{2}^{2}-8{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\  & =(2{x}_{1}^{2}-8{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+9{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2({x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+9{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+9{x}_{2}^{2} & =2([{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+4{x}_{2}^{2}]-4{x}_{2}^{2})+9{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2(({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2})^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2})+9{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2})^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2})+9{x}_{2}^{2} & =2({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2})^{2}-8{x}_{2}^{2}+9{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2})^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n2{y}_{1}^{2}+1{y}_{2}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &={x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2} &={x}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ $1\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404638 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e5218bd-78ef-5fa2-b2a7-66efde9a8122" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$9$ and ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404640} {:answer/id #uuid "bf3f10df-fdfa-56b7-a1de-da199a72f22b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$9$ and ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404641} {:answer/id #uuid "4a6c1183-9409-57f2-97d5-ddf9a03ba804" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ and ${x}_{2}-{x}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404642} {:answer/id #uuid "0e9c2ae1-d2dd-58b7-a6a3-cfd240449ac8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ and ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404643} {:answer/id #uuid "c4f175cf-21e5-5c59-a3e3-5498ae74ba7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ and ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$9$ and ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404640} :answer-field/id #uuid "34930159-fd19-5a7b-abd1-198173eae884" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404639}] :question/id #uuid "106b083d-c143-5f48-8526-3cd804d072e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-94139" :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)=9{x}_{1}^{2}-18{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+16{x}_{2}^{2}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,{y}_{1}^{2}+7{y}_{2}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2} &={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what is missing from the blank spaces?" :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{1}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =9{x}_{1}^{2}-18{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+16{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =(9{x}_{1}^{2}-18{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+16{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =9({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+16{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+16{x}_{2}^{2} & =9([{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}]-{x}_{2}^{2})+16{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =9(({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2})+16{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9(({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2})+16{x}_{2}^{2} & =9({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-9{x}_{2}^{2}+16{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =9({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}+7{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n9{y}_{1}^{2}+7{y}_{2}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &={x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2} &={x}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ $9\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a Quadratic Form to Canonical Form Using Lagrange's Method: 2D-Case"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161996 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161788 :question/id #uuid "f889b145-edc7-5721-ab60-c3395b86e4b9" :question/math-academy-id "e-8186" :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(\\mathbf{x})=x_1^2-4x_3^2+2x_1x_2-4x_1x_3+2x_2x_3$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n![](images/bf/bf0297b0d758d02198d01565050bc5f3b02b0964336d3b84fdca331fabed6051.png)\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?" :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group $x_1^2$-term with all cross-product terms that contain $x_1$ and complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{3}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{3})+2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}))+2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})+({x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2})+2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-4{x}_{3}^{2}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-8{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we group $x_2^2$-term with all cross-product terms that contain $x_2,$ factor out the coefficient of $x_2^2,$ and complete the square inside the second parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}^{2}-6{x}_{2}{x}_{3})-8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}-([{x}_{2}^{2}-6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+9{x}_{3}^{2}]-9{x}_{3}^{2})-8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-3{x}_{3})^{2}+9{x}_{3}^{2}-8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-3{x}_{3})^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n![](images/84/84f88cbb41e573d7ed0793919e0ad25477a46637d09144ca9f462e12f0bc6e90.png)\n\nTherefore, from top to bottom, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\qquad$ $x_1+x_2-2x_3 \\quad$ and $\\quad x_2-3x_3.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13e5e149-54cd-528e-b50e-1cafecb7b77a" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162608 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc9626ab-4ae1-5f47-a4b3-ce0f283d3974" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x_{1} - x_{2} + 3x_{3}$ and $x_{2} - 4x_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160941} {:answer/id #uuid "d34f2d18-6ac5-5a4a-a6b4-8ab35fc9573e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x_{1} - x_{2} - 3x_{3}$ and $x_{2} - 8x_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160942} {:answer/id #uuid "da547e7a-4f8f-56d5-97ea-aeb331edb50c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x_{1} - x_{2} + 3x_{3}$ and $x_{2} + x_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160943} {:answer/id #uuid "e5e56a62-1731-5c76-928e-e9e784635d07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x_{1} - x_{2} - 3x_{3}$ and $x_{2} + 8x_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160944} {:answer/id #uuid "3420c164-ca7a-5e3e-b292-1463c3c940a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x_{1} + x_{2} + 3x_{3}$ and $x_{2} + 4x_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160945}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ad59d4fb-6fc3-56f2-b2f3-aca4c8f86dad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160940}] :question/id #uuid "69960f3d-5ba0-51a2-8eb2-680f0b84bc33" :question/math-academy-id "q-93845" :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x) = x_{1}^{2} - 11x_{3}^{2} - 2x_{1}x_{2} + 6x_{1}x_{3} + 2x_{2}x_{3}$ to the canonical form given below.\n\n$y_{1}^{2} - y_{2}^{2} - 4y_{3}^{2}, {y_{1} = x_{1} - x_{2} + 3x_{3}; y_{2} = x_{2} - 4x_{3}; y_{3} = x_{3}$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162609 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "859716e9-70aa-55fd-b169-7203292282c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x_{1} - 2x_{2} - 4x_{3}$ and $4x_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160947} {:answer/id #uuid "900944ee-bf5d-5006-9c86-e6b72c223745" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x_{1} - x_{2} - 2x_{3}$ and $2x_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160948} {:answer/id #uuid "ecbb8125-e62e-54a1-a83f-ca793d31c3c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x_{1} - x_{2} + 2x_{3}$ and $5x_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160949} {:answer/id #uuid "061ca651-8df8-5254-b2d1-94c6be424830" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x_{1} - 2x_{2} + 4x_{3}$ and $x_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160950} {:answer/id #uuid "07f1d9b0-b090-5184-b775-e29185ba371e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x_{1} - x_{2} - 2x_{3}$ and $x_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160951}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ac551b48-c968-58de-8e97-519b1febbae5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160946} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5d2c0b2-260d-59a8-a622-0edc988f764a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,4{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373395} {:answer/id #uuid "ed8a4e82-2ed7-542d-9c3d-7fa29eb9cba0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,5{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373396} {:answer/id #uuid "d2b8143b-0655-5fa2-9d8d-b272adf49785" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,2{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373397} {:answer/id #uuid "048a936f-1725-5c13-bea4-65127ef9eac2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373398} {:answer/id #uuid "c6086673-4988-5e1a-af21-82e3b6fdac99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373398} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6fbd868-edf2-526c-94a2-f79f0a6a997b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373394}] :question/id #uuid "82badb2c-cae9-57c8-a7d0-945e02ef849b" :question/math-academy-id "q-93852" :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+5{x}_{3}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}+{y}_{3}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2} &=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{3} &={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?" :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+5{x}_{3}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+4{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{3})+4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+5{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}))+4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+5{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})+({x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})^{2})+4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+5{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})^{2}+4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+5{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}-4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-4{x}_{3}^{2}+4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+5{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}+{y}_{3}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &={x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{2} &={x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3} &={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTherefore, top to bottom, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272179 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dee7cba-663b-50e6-924c-0e28fde5b2e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-6{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269389} {:answer/id #uuid "33f5e658-0539-509a-8b95-7e3f776c162a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269743} {:answer/id #uuid "84e63b7e-d4bb-5cd6-868b-f474573666af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270418} {:answer/id #uuid "c6ec68c0-4771-55d7-9893-3ea93f85c615" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271021} {:answer/id #uuid "cc300f21-bcc9-5526-847a-6676ce5447dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271061}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271061} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ff565ae-2bfb-56bb-b477-8e1c8d5ecdc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271595}] :question/id #uuid "1d1b69b2-59ef-5c2d-94c0-d1ed23d06b2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-140986" :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+40{x}_{3}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+12{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}+8{y}_{3}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2} &=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{3} &={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?" :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+40{x}_{3}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+12{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+12{x}_{1}{x}_{3})-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+40{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}-6{x}_{3}))-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+40{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}-6{x}_{3})+({x}_{2}-6{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-6{x}_{3})^{2})-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+40{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-6{x}_{3})^{2}-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+40{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+12{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-36{x}_{3}^{2}-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+40{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+4{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we group ${x}_{2}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{2},$ factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{2}^{2},$ and complete the square inside the second parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}^{2}-4{x}_{2}{x}_{3})+4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3})^{2}-([{x}_{2}^{2}-4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+4{x}_{3}^{2}]-4{x}_{3}^{2})+4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}+8{y}_{3}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &={x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{2} &={x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{3} &={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTherefore, from top to bottom, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357676 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "373941e6-dfef-5c2a-b2e1-19164dc8112b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355161} {:answer/id #uuid "3a8f640b-b10e-5a5c-b0d3-7b814d9ffaf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,2{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355193} {:answer/id #uuid "3c643044-ecf6-578e-a53f-fde3d463b597" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,5{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355206} {:answer/id #uuid "562414d5-a6e5-5db8-bec6-b0adfc4c4286" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355433} {:answer/id #uuid "e8e6b93a-1b37-5e41-8cc2-eaa6850b46f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,2{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356699}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355433} :answer-field/id #uuid "907c65a0-992e-507c-acb6-654d9d4515fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357174}] :question/id #uuid "26c07eb8-f4ba-54ff-8eb0-e8e9547c992b" :question/math-academy-id "q-94161" :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+26{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2}-10{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-10{x}_{2}{x}_{3}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}+2{y}_{3}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2} &=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{3} &={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?" :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+26{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2}-10{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-10{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-10{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3})-10{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+26{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}(5{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}))-10{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+26{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}(5{x}_{2}-{x}_{3})+(5{x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2}-(5{x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2})-10{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+26{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}-(5{x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2}-10{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+26{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}-25{x}_{2}^{2}+10{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}^{2}-10{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+26{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}+2{y}_{3}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &={x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{2} &={x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3} &={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTherefore, top to bottom, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357677 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ac3e9f2-3152-5fef-80ac-e6ef289f7d74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355024} {:answer/id #uuid "5bc803cd-d665-5e94-bea8-75a7e9e963cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355474} {:answer/id #uuid "6f786984-351f-5785-84fa-84d6975041c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355650} {:answer/id #uuid "f86a41b2-cc4f-5af4-bcce-d25831ef478d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356829} {:answer/id #uuid "fbb01322-6260-5ffe-aa3a-50fb1e6e3974" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355024} :answer-field/id #uuid "9521daa1-ff32-5e44-a503-de2f0e698bbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357183}] :question/id #uuid "92c3ad7d-ccc9-522a-9c03-058c009432f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-94162" :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}-2{y}_{3}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2} &=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{3} &={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?" :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3})+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}+{x}_{3}))+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}+{x}_{3})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2})+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we group ${x}_{2}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{2},$ factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{2}^{2},$ and complete the square inside the second parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3})-{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+([{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+{x}_{3}^{2}]-{x}_{3}^{2})-{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2}-2{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}-2{y}_{3}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &={x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{2} &={x}_{2}-{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{3} &={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTherefore, from top to bottom, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371845 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "260c3288-049c-56e5-9c05-d3104f66d56d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371847} {:answer/id #uuid "c29c4c0a-bdbe-569d-a8c8-66e7234cb131" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371848} {:answer/id #uuid "1e1eef42-db92-5d9d-9986-178c9c0a5255" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}$ and $2{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371849} {:answer/id #uuid "e6bb4bf4-f423-5fc3-a10a-b5e64ede2f6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}$ and $-{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371850} {:answer/id #uuid "d40a16c7-4b2c-52b8-a716-2788797d1562" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}$ and $-2{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371848} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fc57af7-337a-5abd-a655-8c9d0c3bc923" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371846}] :question/id #uuid "3522e8d1-6c11-5e87-ac91-d34c9481ad13" :question/math-academy-id "q-140985" :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+10{x}_{3}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+16{x}_{2}{x}_{3}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}-4{y}_{2}^{2}-6{y}_{3}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2} &=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{3} &={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?" :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+10{x}_{3}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+16{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{3})+16{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+10{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}({x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}))+16{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+10{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}({x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})+4({x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})^{2}-4({x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})^{2})+16{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+10{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+2({x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}))^{2}-4({x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})^{2}+16{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+10{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3})^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2}-16{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-16{x}_{3}^{2}+16{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+10{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3})^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2}-6{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}-4{y}_{2}^{2}-6{y}_{3}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &={x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{2} &={x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3} &={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTherefore, top to bottom, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404651 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03cd7e59-1e44-587f-b46a-21c18b58dde4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,4{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404653} {:answer/id #uuid "3efc6564-edbb-5052-ae42-15c048d414c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,2{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404654} {:answer/id #uuid "3e9edbfc-9f58-5309-aeeb-e8e499106697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,2{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404655} {:answer/id #uuid "2fc2a336-4159-5066-a3cd-4b8a29a174eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404656} {:answer/id #uuid "4316b229-faa7-58df-b15d-4a8b761dc778" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404657} :answer-field/id #uuid "b31630c8-ab94-5333-9ad7-cc37ed818916" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404652}] :question/id #uuid "8abbbd8d-56c6-5a50-8378-69e23e070d79" :question/math-academy-id "q-94159" :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+18{x}_{3}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}+2{y}_{3}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2} &=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{3} &={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?" :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+18{x}_{3}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{3})-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+18{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}))-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+18{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}-4{x}_{3})+({x}_{2}-4{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-4{x}_{3})^{2})-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+18{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-4{x}_{3})^{2}-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+18{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-16{x}_{3}^{2}-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+18{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}+2{y}_{3}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &={x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{2} &={x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3} &={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTherefore, top to bottom, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404658 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b01913ba-1ad0-59a0-871e-90a0411bf3a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404660} {:answer/id #uuid "4d7db0e5-68d0-5987-a213-b46b03bf8fbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404661} {:answer/id #uuid "43a4545f-8225-54d6-9b1a-1fecbf7d9030" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404662} {:answer/id #uuid "1767a169-7f64-5caa-94be-89476370b897" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404663} {:answer/id #uuid "112340bd-0af7-5ff3-914b-13b07c9b01e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404664}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404664} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a95c5f5-400e-5bc7-8b8f-25788f5bde1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404659}] :question/id #uuid "c34790ce-c36b-5dcb-a189-d84001cf999a" :question/math-academy-id "q-94179" :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}+2{y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{3}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2} &=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{3} &={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?" :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3})+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}-{x}_{3}))+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}-{x}_{3})+({x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2})+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}-{x}_{3})^{2}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}^{2}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+7{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we group ${x}_{2}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{2},$ factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{2}^{2},$ and complete the square inside the second parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2({x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{2}{x}_{3})+7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2([{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+4{x}_{3}^{2}]-4{x}_{3}^{2})+7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2(({x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})^{2}-4{x}_{3}^{2})+7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2({x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})^{2}-8{x}_{3}^{2}+7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3})^{2}+2({x}_{2}+2{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}+2{y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{3}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &={x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{2} &={x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{3} &={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTherefore, from top to bottom, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404665 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50b9470b-2754-554a-a9c2-925ecf2d9815" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404667} {:answer/id #uuid "79527219-621e-5317-b458-17d0d4848f04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404668} {:answer/id #uuid "5407e66c-32a1-5546-8d23-7a3898c552bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404669} {:answer/id #uuid "05e9aef9-07d4-524e-96c9-353a90baec85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404670} {:answer/id #uuid "236bfa03-ae3f-5274-91ff-5664d7e0e391" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404671}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404667} :answer-field/id #uuid "10ef20bf-2e5d-50b3-b950-69a099e3e7b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404666}] :question/id #uuid "190daf82-0a4f-5d1d-bcce-07f33dc7233c" :question/math-academy-id "q-94213" :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+14{x}_{2}{x}_{3}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}-2{y}_{2}^{2}+{y}_{3}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2} &=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{3} &={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?" :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+14{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{3})+14{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}))+14{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})+({x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})^{2})+14{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})^{2}+14{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}-6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-9{x}_{3}^{2}+14{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})^{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-7{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we group ${x}_{2}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{2},$ factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{2}^{2},$ and complete the square inside the second parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})^{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})^{2}-2({x}_{2}^{2}-4{x}_{2}{x}_{3})-7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})^{2}-2([{x}_{2}^{2}-4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+4{x}_{3}^{2}]-4{x}_{3}^{2})-7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})^{2}-2(({x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}-4{x}_{3}^{2})-7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})^{2}-2({x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2}-7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})^{2}-2({x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}-2{y}_{2}^{2}+{y}_{3}^{2},\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &={x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{2} &={x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{3} &={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTherefore, from top to bottom, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a Quadratic Form to Canonical Form Using Lagrange's Method: 3D-Case"}] :topic/math-academy-id 3124 :topic/title "Finding the Canonical Form of a Quadratic Form Using Lagrange's Method"}] [{:activity/_scope [{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129982} :activity/id #uuid "427e5f35-5438-583c-9454-df8e3ae0c517" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129982 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130356 :tutorial/content "A square matrix $A$ is **block diagonalizable** if it is similar to a block diagonal matrix $B.$ That is, there exists a block diagonal matrix $B$ and an invertible matrix $P$ such that\n\n$$\nA=PBP^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFor example, the matrix \n\n![](images/18/1857eb7b5b094ae9cdb3c233be3513e1c9a725d68d104145db573f02be065340.svg) \n\nis block diagonalizable because it can be factored as follows:\n\n![](images/43/43f25f96d39e392d7b1b0910eee54650e6b3c1a977c0cc43c4c04aebe2f4b085.svg)\n\nHere, the matrix $A$ has eigenvalues \n\n$$\n{\\color{red}\\lambda_1 = 2},\\qquad \n{\\color{blue}\\lambda_2=3-2\\textrm i},\\qquad \n{\\color{blue}\\lambda_3=3+2\\textrm i}.\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\lambda_2 = \\overline{\\lambda_3}.$\nThe eigenvectors of ${\\color{red}\\lambda_1}, {\\color{blue}\\lambda_2},$ and ${\\color{blue}\\lambda_3},$ respectively, are\n\n![](images/a9/a91e32ad98d0b2bf93053745873fd219c2ed6fbd533c3e8a974032d63feea161.svg)\n\nAgain, notice that $\\mathbf{v}_2 = \\overline{\\mathbf{v}_3}.$\nThe first column of $P$ corresponds to the eigenvector ${\\color{red}\\mathbf{v}_1},$ and the second and third columns correspond to the real and the imaginary parts of ${\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v}_2}.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "8edf8405-33c8-5922-8946-6f87b2881781" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3597 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "2079dce9-f014-5601-a83c-150fae42ef41" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129984}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129983 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129137 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d4c1a7b-2341-5b8c-8112-0290f8eda65f"} :step/id #uuid "6045c7fa-0f99-5ffd-9594-e626c92e4020" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129985}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129984 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130357 :tutorial/content "We have the following theorem regarding the block diagonalization of a real $3\\!\\times\\! 3$ matrix:\n\n*If $A$ is a real $3\\times 3$ matrix with one real eigenvalue ${\\color{red}\\lambda_1}$ with corresponding eigenvector ${\\color{red}{\\mathbf{v}_1}},$ and two complex eigenvalues ${\\color{blue}\\lambda_2} = \\overline{\\color{blue}\\lambda}_{\\color{blue}3}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v}_2} = \\overline{\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v}}_{\\color{blue}3},$ then* \n\n$$\nA=PBP^{-1},\n$$\n\n*where the matrices $B$ and $P$ are given by*\n![](images/97/97adc950e68b3e7bce042b741e7b0a33f4baa2f9aae91f9bb40b4bbe36b0b595.svg)\n\nIn other words, if $A$ is a real $3\\!\\times\\! 3$ matrix with one real eigenvalue and two complex eigenvalues, then $A$ is block diagonalizable.\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The block of $B$ constructed from the real and imaginary parts of $\\color{blue}\\lambda_2$ is a rotation-scaling matrix.\n\n- We can write the blocks of $B$ in either order. However, the order of the columns of $P$ *must* correspond to the order of the blocks." :tutorial/id #uuid "56c5960d-6197-586e-850e-8f1a23e2289a" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3598 :tutorial/title "The Block Diagonalization Theorem for a 3x3 Matrix"} :step/id #uuid "9ac92ee1-74aa-5b6d-a07e-d4fc3f68f30b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130015}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129985 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129138 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d9a65788-ff15-58e9-8329-c69b2a8e311b"} :step/id #uuid "5d6954b7-9d4b-57e8-aee6-999d162199be" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129986}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129986 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130358 :tutorial/content "We can find a block diagonalization for any real $n\\!\\times\\! n$ matrix $A.$ This means that for any square matrix $A,$ we can construct a block diagonal matrix $B$ and invertible matrix $P$ such that \n\n$$\nA=PBP^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere the blocks of $B$ are either:\n\n- $1\\!\\times\\! 1$ blocks containing the real eigenvalues of $A,$ or\n\n- $2\\!\\times\\! 2$ blocks containing the rotation-scaling matrices corresponding to the complex (not real) eigenvalues of $A.$\n\nThe columns of $P$ form bases of the eigenspaces for the real eigenvectors, or come in the pairs $\\left(\\textrm{Re}(\\mathbf{v}), \\textrm{Im}(\\mathbf{v})\\right)$ for the non-real eigenvectors.\n\nLet's see an example of block diagonalization for higher-dimensional matrices." :tutorial/id #uuid "650f30ea-d42a-5fba-bd00-3f269007df84" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3599 :tutorial/title "Generalization of Block Diagonalization to NxN Matrices"} :step/id #uuid "695a49a5-60af-5017-b281-1870ceb33c6d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129987}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129987 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129139 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5ccd12c-a814-5ebb-985c-eef8707001f0"} :step/id #uuid "d7512dc9-649d-5cd3-992b-9f3d84b178e3"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130015 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129160 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6704692a-2219-559f-9352-97c5fb590894"} :step/id #uuid "9a08b734-6db2-5bf9-8aae-178359e681f6" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129983}}] :activity/title "Block Diagonalization of NxN Matrices" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186129362}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186050593 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129137 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128948 :question/id #uuid "1cc03cef-e717-5ac1-ab9d-75508f3aa056" :question/math-academy-id "e-5533" :question/problem "![](images/75/750197747be9a845e1db31b969d333edbbebf7a28ce85bcb61752ff29a872f83.svg)\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above. Find a block diagonal matrix $B,$ where the $2 \\times 2$ block represents a rotation-scaling matrix, such that $A=PBP^{-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A$ is a real $3\\times 3$ matrix that has one real eigenvalue ${\\color{red}\\lambda_1}$ with corresponding eigenvector ${\\color{red}{\\mathbf{v}_1}},$ and two complex eigenvalues ${\\color{blue}\\lambda_2} = \\overline{\\color{blue}\\lambda}_{\\color{blue}3}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v}_2} = \\overline{\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v}}_{\\color{blue}3},$ then $A=PBP^{-1},$ where\n![](images/ab/abd031651857b6c66be090b1f3dc9cdeaff19ea1adac50dbfe234f0414f6afb1.svg)\nSwapping the blocks on the main diagonal of $B$ will result in switching the corresponding columns in $P.$\n\nTo compute the eigenvalues of $A,$ we solve the characteristic equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-2-\\lambda  & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1-\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )((-2-\\lambda )^{2}-1(-1)) & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the real eigenvalue is \n$\\lambda_1={\\color{red}-1}.$\nNow, using the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{2,3} & =\\frac{-4\\pm \\sqrt{(4)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 5}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4\\pm \\sqrt{-4}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4\\pm 2\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =-2\\pm \\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the block diagonal matrix is\n\n![](images/b0/b0fe98cefcd9a911ba02684ff93696bc14f468729d73d07055a7a1638c44f4ef.svg)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d4c1a7b-2341-5b8c-8112-0290f8eda65f" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129683 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cdc86f5e-ee0e-5f5b-bb53-b0d9d642e561" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127580} {:answer/id #uuid "cf456291-bf1b-5e49-a096-1aa9ce1c9142" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127581} {:answer/id #uuid "f3525f2b-4d2d-5a9d-8915-62d104f33b56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127582} {:answer/id #uuid "19b54e4a-2e7b-5d74-914f-3e5820dbbecc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127583} {:answer/id #uuid "264f2dd8-d08c-5e40-adc9-c78425eee4c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127584}] :answer-field/id #uuid "765fc465-f6b6-5a0a-aefe-7473f304bfba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127579} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47e55c69-1866-588d-872a-b402386f3e06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368516} {:answer/id #uuid "aaf80517-57f1-595e-a0c6-e931586cc9b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368517} {:answer/id #uuid "d3509644-e4ea-51d2-a471-d35c123da88d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368518} {:answer/id #uuid "00e54f49-e547-573b-a5d0-5831fa66ad14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368519} {:answer/id #uuid "6e481d77-a41c-5160-be87-d2c659c36170" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368520}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368519} :answer-field/id #uuid "38d5c140-2980-57f5-9c02-49b92c04d215" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368515}] :question/id #uuid "58dcf2b4-e0ab-52d4-9f82-d78c5ef8a397" :question/math-academy-id "q-38655" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above. Find a block diagonal matrix $B,$ where the $2\\times 2$ block represents a rotation-scaling matrix, such that $A=PB{P}^{-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A$ is a real $3\\times 3$ matrix that has one real eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}$ with corresponding eigenvector ${v}_{1},$ and two complex eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{3}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{3},$ then $A=PB{P}^{-1},$ where\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}{\\lambda }_{1} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\text{Re}({\\lambda }_{2}) & \\text{Im}({\\lambda }_{2}) \\\\ 0 & -\\text{Im}({\\lambda }_{2}) & \\text{Re}({\\lambda }_{2})\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\,P=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ {v}_{1} & \\text{Re}({v}_{2}) & \\text{Im}({v}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSwapping the blocks on the main diagonal of $B$ will result in switching the corresponding columns in $P.$\n\nTo compute the eigenvalues of $A,$ we solve the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1-\\lambda  & 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3-\\lambda  & 6 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )((1-\\lambda )^{2}-1(-1)) & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the real eigenvalue is \n${\\lambda }_{1}=3.$\nNow, using the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{2,3} & =\\frac{2\\pm \\sqrt{(-2)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm \\sqrt{-4}}{2} \\\\  & =1\\pm \\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the block diagonal matrix is\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129687 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "860f72c7-8aee-5df4-8733-468b8bcd9a56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127604} {:answer/id #uuid "98229294-9497-5e7a-b740-6d2291e30615" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127605} {:answer/id #uuid "e3576899-7848-5c19-8ea1-7ffc48abfccb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127606} {:answer/id #uuid "05d3a1c7-4e97-5ba7-a775-64d6ec5eaf10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :