 corresponding columns in $P.$\n\nTo compute the eigenvalues of $A,$ we solve the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}8-\\lambda  & 0 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -3-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ -10 & 0 & 4-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-3-\\lambda )((8-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-2(-10)) & =0 \\\\ (-3-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-12\\lambda +52) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the real eigenvalue is \n${\\lambda }_{1}=-3.$\nNow, using the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{2,3} & =\\frac{12\\pm \\sqrt{(-12)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 52}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pm \\sqrt{-64}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pm 8\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =6\\pm 4\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the block diagonal matrix is\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269078 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b8c81ff-4fba-5662-9d08-3e487f024917" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266814} {:answer/id #uuid "670db349-289c-59c6-92ff-3b70af48ecc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267059} {:answer/id #uuid "9ed5f3c0-e1f4-5079-9eb6-011ae7b51c8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267576} {:answer/id #uuid "d0cd01a2-51bc-5011-b65e-f6c8137a55cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268010} {:answer/id #uuid "e8ee0fa6-ec3c-5515-be0f-532aac7019ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 